# GovernanceRule: entity of the GovernanceRules accelerator. A standard data governance rule that every MDM project of the company must apply, written as an imperative RFC 2119 statement (MUST, SHOULD, MAY), with its...
_package: GovernanceRules.entities.GovernanceRule
_type: Entity
_name: GovernanceRule
label: Governance rule
pluralLabel: Governance rules
physicalTableName: GOV_RULE
entityType: BASIC
description: 'A standard data governance rule that every MDM project of the company must apply, written as an imperative RFC
  2119 statement (MUST, SHOULD, MAY), with its category, the implementation pattern a designer uses to apply it, its scopes
  (data domain, data classification, attribute type) and the regulations or standards it cites. Authored by the governance
  stewards and approved by the governance owner through the Rule review workflow; each approved version is kept in the history.


  AI agent instructions: Only rules with InForce = true apply to a design. Cite the rule Code (for example PRIV-003) in the
  description of every object that implements the rule. RequirementLevel MUST is mandatory, SHOULD is expected unless justified,
  MAY is optional. Never apply or cite a rule that is not in force. When you design or change a data product, first call the
  AttributeTypeCatalog named query to classify each attribute you touch (attribute type code, default classification), then call
  RuleChecklist once for the whole change with the data domain, the classifications and the attribute type codes as comma-separated
  lists (ApplicableRules returns the same rules for one attribute type with their statements and citations); use RuleDetail for one
  rule and RulesByCategory to browse a category. Lists of values store codes (MUST, SHOULD, MAY; PRIVACY, DATA_QUALITY...): filter
  on the code. Always pass the data domain: an omitted parameter only matches rules that are not restricted on that dimension, so
  industry-specific rules (for example pharma rules scoped to MEDICINAL_PRODUCT, HCP, CLINICAL_SITE or to pharma attribute types
  such as NDC or NPI) only come back when your design names those domains or attribute types.'
historizeGolden: true
historizeMaster: false
enableDelete: false
primaryKey: GovernanceRules.entities.GovernanceRule.GovernanceRule.Code
sourceIdGeneration:
  mode: MANUAL
attributes:
- _type: EntityAttribute
  _name: Code
  label: Code
  physicalName: GR_CODE
  dataType: String
  length: 40
  mandatory: true
  description: 'Natural key of the rule; its prefix follows the category: DQ-, PRIV-, SEC-, RET-, REF-, MDM-, META-, AI-,
    STW-, MOD-, entered by the author and never changed (for example PRIV-003).'
  mandatoryValidationScope: PRE_CONSO
- _type: EntityAttribute
  _name: Title
  label: Title
  physicalName: GR_TITLE
  dataType: String
  length: 200
  mandatory: true
  description: Short title of the rule.
  mandatoryValidationScope: PRE_CONSO
- _type: EntityAttribute
  _name: Statement
  label: Statement
  physicalName: GR_STATEMENT
  dataType: String
  length: 4000
  mandatory: true
  description: Normative text of the rule, an imperative sentence in RFC 2119 style (MUST, SHOULD, MAY).
  mandatoryValidationScope: PRE_CONSO
- _type: EntityAttribute
  _name: Rationale
  label: Rationale
  physicalName: GR_RATIONALE
  dataType: String
  length: 4000
  mandatory: false
  description: 'Why the rule exists: the risk it addresses or the regulation it serves.'
- _type: EntityAttribute
  _name: RequirementLevel
  label: Requirement level
  physicalName: GR_LEVEL
  dataType: GovernanceRules.list_of_values.RequirementLevel
  lovValidationScope: PRE_CONSO
  mandatory: true
  description: Strength of the rule, code MUST (Must), SHOULD (Should) or MAY (May), as in RFC 2119.
  mandatoryValidationScope: PRE_CONSO
- _type: EntityAttribute
  _name: Category
  label: Category
  physicalName: GR_CATEGORY
  dataType: GovernanceRules.list_of_values.RuleCategory
  lovValidationScope: PRE_CONSO
  mandatory: true
  description: Category of the rule, code DATA_QUALITY, PRIVACY, SECURITY_ACCESS, RETENTION, REFERENCE_DATA, IDENTITY_MATCHING,
    METADATA_DOCUMENTATION, AI_USAGE, STEWARDSHIP or MODELING_CONVENTIONS.
  mandatoryValidationScope: PRE_CONSO
- _type: EntityAttribute
  _name: ImplementationPattern
  label: Implementation pattern
  physicalName: GR_PATTERN
  dataType: GovernanceRules.list_of_values.ImplementationPattern
  lovValidationScope: PRE_CONSO
  mandatory: false
  description: How a designer implements the rule in a data product, code VALIDATION, ENRICHER, PRIVILEGE_ROW_FILTER, MATCHING_SURVIVORSHIP,
    WORKFLOW, RETENTION_POLICY, DESCRIPTION_AI_INSTRUCTION, NAMING_CONVENTION or REFERENCE_ENTITY.
- _type: EntityAttribute
  _name: ImplementationGuidance
  label: Implementation guidance
  physicalName: GR_GUIDANCE
  dataType: String
  length: 4000
  mandatory: false
  description: 'Concrete guidance for the designer: what to build in the data product to comply with the rule.'
- _type: EntityAttribute
  _name: Example
  label: Example
  physicalName: GR_EXAMPLE
  dataType: String
  length: 4000
  mandatory: false
  description: An example of a compliant implementation or value.
- _type: EntityAttribute
  _name: LifecycleStatus
  label: Status
  physicalName: GR_STATUS
  dataType: GovernanceRules.list_of_values.LifecycleStatus
  lovValidationScope: PRE_CONSO
  mandatory: true
  description: Lifecycle status, code DRAFT (Draft), IN_REVIEW (In review), APPROVED (Approved), RETIREMENT_REQUESTED (Retirement
    requested) or RETIRED (Retired). Changed by the Rule review workflow.
  mandatoryValidationScope: PRE_CONSO
- _type: EntityAttribute
  _name: EffectiveDate
  label: Effective date
  physicalName: GR_EFFECTIVE
  dataType: Date
  mandatory: false
  description: Date from which the rule applies.
- _type: EntityAttribute
  _name: RetirementDate
  label: Retirement date
  physicalName: GR_RETIREMENT
  dataType: Date
  mandatory: false
  description: Date from which the rule no longer applies; empty while the rule is not retired.
- _type: EntityAttribute
  _name: RetirementReason
  label: Retirement reason
  physicalName: GR_RET_REASON
  dataType: String
  length: 1000
  mandatory: false
  description: Why the rule is retired, entered when the retirement is requested.
- _type: EntityAttribute
  _name: ApprovedOn
  label: Approved on
  physicalName: GR_APPROVED_ON
  dataType: Date
  mandatory: false
  description: Date of the last approval by the governance owner.
- _type: EntityAttribute
  _name: ApprovedBy
  label: Approved by
  physicalName: GR_APPROVED_BY
  dataType: String
  length: 128
  mandatory: false
  description: User who gave the last approval.
- _type: EntityAttribute
  _name: InForce
  label: In force
  physicalName: GR_IN_FORCE
  dataType: Boolean
  length: 1
  mandatory: false
  description: 'Computed: true when the status is APPROVED, the effective date is reached and the retirement date, if any,
    is not reached. Computed when the rule is certified.'
